<div type="edition" xml:lang="san-Latn" rendition="class:83231 maturity:83211">
   <p><lb n="1"/>namo jaimanaye stanayitnave svā<add place="below">hā</add></p>
</div>
         <div type="translation" resp="part:kuch">
 	<p n="1">Hommage to Jaimini <supplied reason="subaudible">and</supplied> thunder! Hail! <!-- or Homage to Jaimani! Hail to thunder! --></p>
         </div>
        <div type="commentary">
            <p>On the four corners of the slab, there are carvings of two tridents, a conch and a disc. These are attributes of Śiva and Viṣṇu. 
            On the name Jaimani and its connection to lightning strike, see <ref target="DHARMA_INSCIC00175.xml">C. 175</ref>.
            </p>
         </div>
        <div type="bibliography">
          <p>Preliminary edition by Kunthea Chhom based on the photograph of the stone AMPP 001036, which was published on the cover of BEFEO 90-91 (2003-2004).</p> 
        </div>
